### Email Verification Flow Test
### Make sure Redis and MongoDB are running before testing

### 1. Register a new user (will send email verification)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "username": "newuser123",
  "password": "TestPass123!",
  "firstname": "New",
  "lastname": "User"
}

### 2. Verify email with OTP (replace 123456 with actual OTP from email)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 3. Resend verification email
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com"
}

### 4. Try to register with same email (should fail)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "username": "anotheruser",
  "password": "TestPass123!",
  "firstname": "Another",
  "lastname": "User"
}

### 5. Try to resend verification for already verified email (should fail)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com"
}

### 6. Test with invalid OTP
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "otp": "000000"
}

### 7. Test rate limiting (make multiple requests quickly)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com"
}

### 8. Login after email verification
POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newuser123",
  "password": "TestPass123!"
}
